"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2025-06-20T14:52:08Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T01:33:00Z","closed_at":"2025-06-22T09:35:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107767","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107767","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107767.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107767.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fix the stencil mask combinations to allow both `Read` and `Write` to be toggled at the same time.\r\n\r\nI was using the new outline preset which creates a material with `Read` and `Write` enabled. But when I saved the material and adjusted it, the flags suddenly stopped me from enabling this combination again, instead only enabling `Read`.\r\n\r\nWith this PR, the flag state can now be set to:\r\n- Each flag individually enabled\r\n- `Read` and `Write`\r\n- `Read` and `Write Depth Fail`\r\n- `Write` and `Write Depth Fail`\r\n\r\nI believe my change simply added the `Read` and `Write` combination. And so these should be the valid states of the flag, but please let me know if any of them are invalid!","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"h